<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Whether you are moving your car to a new city or transporting it for business, compliance with transport regulations is non-negotiable.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The foundation of any successful vehicle shipment in India relies on having the correct mandatory paperwork ready before the vehicle is loaded onto a car carrier truck.</span></li></ul>
<p>This ensures that the transporter can legally move your asset without interference from traffic police or customs authorities. Understanding these documents helps you verify the legitimacy of the logistics provider and protects your investment throughout the journey.</p>

<p>Each document serves a specific legal and operational purpose. The registration certificate proves ownership and road legality, while insurance covers potential transit damage. In India, interstate or even long-distance intrastate movement often requires an e-Way bill, especially for commercial vehicles or high-value goods.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Furthermore, a valid GST invoice is crucial for tax compliance, particularly when the shipment involves a business entity.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>If the vehicle is not in the name of the shipper, an owner’s consent letter is vital to authorize the transport.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Failing to present any of these documents can result in the vehicle being impounded or significant fines being levied.</span></li></ul>

<p>When engaging a professional car carrier truck India service, ask them to verify your documents before pickup. This proactive step ensures that the logistics team is fully equipped to handle any checkpoints. Here is the comprehensive checklist of mandatory paperwork you must prepare:</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Registration Certificate (RC):</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The original RC book or a valid digital copy. This is the primary proof of vehicle ownership and roadworthiness. Ensure the name on the RC matches the shipper or has a valid transfer document.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Insurance Policy:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A comprehensive insurance certificate covering transit damage. Verify that the policy is active and includes coverage for third-party liability and own-damage during the vehicle’s movement.</p>
